6.12 Rule 64 of the 2019 Rules provides that in terms  of power made under sub-section (30B) of the MMDR Act  1957, the State Government may, if necessary in public interest,
for the purposes of trial of all or any of the offences under this  rule, either appoint or designate in every district of the State,
special court(s) in consultation with the Chief Justice of the  High Court.
